IFC Canvas modification to the ThatOpen web-ifc JavaScript API
(https://github.com/ThatOpen/engine_web-ifc).

Base: the dist file web-ifc-api-iife.js of the npm package web-ifc@0.0.77
  (https://registry.npmjs.org/web-ifc/-/web-ifc-0.0.77.tgz,
  dist.integrity sha512-VzQ0W/Iiqbidxn1ECUvz6qJ6p2sXBVNcOsUOBCETzy77psAH6yFLKQm74aXabkx3JH4OvFVHe8k1qS6+Z2zl1w==).
  Base file sha256:    684155219a10a3d9e5c51be559489eab29a6168e5a2710eedafaf00309659e5c (6084544 bytes)
  Patched file sha256: 92ed95a3064af65582623e8beb96ec330fa8c8ea40e884960d521a1ead0fd08f (6084709 bytes)
  The change was made directly in that generated bundle, so this diff against
  the npm file is the Source Code Form of the modification. web-ifc.wasm from
  the same package is shipped unmodified
  (sha256 392b547232aa63df84961d9d3d6e2a7a259cd832b888830cab2ee30778bf28a0).

Change: in IfcAPI.Init(), the options object passed to the Emscripten module
  factory WebIFCWasm() is built as a local moduleConfig and, when
  globalThis.__webIfcWasmBinary is set, receives it as wasmBinary (a standard
  Emscripten Module option). This lets the embedding app hand a preloaded
  WebAssembly binary to the Emscripten module instead of having the module
  fetch web-ifc.wasm through locateFile; IFC Canvas loads its viewer page in
  an embedded web view and supplies the bytes of web-ifc.wasm itself. When the
  global is not set, behaviour is identical to upstream.

License: MPL-2.0, the license of web-ifc itself (see LICENSE.md in the npm
  package and at the root of the web-ifc source tree).

Apply: in a directory that holds the npm web-ifc-api-iife.js, run
  git apply web-ifc-0.0.77-api-iife.patch    (or: patch -p1 < web-ifc-0.0.77-api-iife.patch)

